2026-10-31T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2387) 'The double.yml matrix and the release
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2387  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2387) '`.github/workflows/double.yml` runs on each `v0.0.0-<UTC time>-<commit>` tag the assembler pushes to entities-zone, and on a dispatch with `release_tag` set. It builds the tagged tree in a matrix of `windows-x86_64` (llvm-mingw 20260922, `use_mingw=yes use_llvm=yes`), `linux-x86_64` and `macos-arm64`, each at `precision=double` for `target=editor` and `target=template_release` (`debug_symbols=yes` on the Windows template, for the fault below), with sccache on the runner's cache. It publishes the six binaries and their sha256s as a release on the tag.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2387  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2387) 'Replaying a job on a desk
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2387  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-31T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2387) 'The escript in &{repo("service-godot-build")} takes `--precision` and `--extra`, so the Windows job replays on a Windows desk when a runner is not at hand. The pen's `CITATION.cff` records the engine commit, the toolchain, the flag line and each sha256. The Frame pulls the Windows release with `curl` over `ssh frame` into `~/rfd2287/godot-dbl`. This Mac pulls the macOS one.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2387  1 LINE
 Text:Written

